## Why This Is Asked
Assesses advanced AWS ABAC, cross-account governance, and policy-as-code in a multi-tenant data lake; targets practical use of IAM Identity Center, PrincipalTags, Lake Formation, and a GitOps deployment flow.

## Key Concepts
- ABAC with session/principal tags
- Lake Formation fine-grained permissions
- Cross-account policy deployment (GitOps)
- Revocation latency and audits (CloudTrail, Config, Access Analyzer)

## Code Example
```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": { "Federated": "arn:aws:iam::123456789012:saml-provider/AWS_SSO" },
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id": "tenant-A"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject", "s3:ListBucket"],
      "Resource": [
        "arn:aws:s3:::data-lake",
        "arn:aws:s3:::data-lake/tenant-A/*"
      ],
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": { "s3:prefix": "tenant-A/" }
      }
    },
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["lakeformation:GetDataLocation", "lakeformation:GetTable", "lakeformation:GrantPermissions", "glue:GetDatabase", "glue:GetTable"],
      "Resource": "*",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": { "aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id": "tenant-A" }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test revocation latency end-to-end? 
- How would you scale this across many tenants and regions?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design data residency controls, cross-region analytics, and automated tenant lifecycle in a scalable, secure way. Requires reasoning about IAM boundaries, per-tenant data segregation, and disaster recovery trade-offs.

## Key Concepts

- Data residency and tenant isolation
- Region-bound storage and access controls
- Serverless analytics stack (Lambda, Glue, Athena/Redshift)
- Automated onboarding/offboarding (CDK/Terraform)
- Cross-region dashboards and DR strategy (RTO/RPO)

## Code Example

```javascript
// CDK sketch (simplified)
const bucket = new s3.Bucket(this, 'TenantBucket', {
  encryption: s3.BucketEncryption.S3_MANAGED,
  removalPolicy: RemovalPolicy.RETAIN
});
bucket.addToResourcePolicy(new PolicyStatement({
  principals: [new ArnPrincipal('*')],
  actions: ['s3:*'],
  resources: [bucket.bucketArn + '/*'],
  conditions: { StringEquals: { 'aws:PrincipalOrgID': 'o-abc' } }
}));
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate data residency across tenants in CI/CD?
- What a/b tests would you run to compare cross-region analytics performance?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses ABAC, cross-account trust, per-tenant encryption, and test rigor for production-grade data lakes.

## Key Concepts
- ABAC with IAM tags and S3 object tags
- Per-tenant KMS CMKs and encryption context
- Cross-account role with least privilege
- Test plan including canaries and revocation

## Code Example
```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject","s3:ListBucket"],
      "Resource": [
        "arn:aws:s3:::telemetry-lake/tenant-id=${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}/*"
      ],
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "s3:ExistingObjectTag/tenant-id": "${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["kms:Decrypt","kms:Encrypt","kms:GenerateDataKey*"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:kms:region:acct:key/<tenant-id-CMK-arn>",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "kms:EncryptionContext:tenant-id": "${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```
